spans.s:
प्र-√ शंस् P. Ā. -शंसति, ˚ते, (irreg. Pot. -शंसीयात्, Cāṇ.), to proclaim, declare, praise, laud, extol, RV. &c. &c.;
to urge on, stimulate, RV. i, 84, 19;
to approve, esteem, value (with न, to disapprove, blame), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to foretell, prophesy, Cāṇ.

प्र-√ सद् P. -सीदति (ep. also Ā. ˚ते), to fall into the power of (acc.), MaitrS.; AitBr.;
to settle down, grow clear and bright, become placid or tranquil (as the sea or sky, met. applied to the mind), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to become clear or distinct, KaṭhUp.; Kām.;
to become satisfied or pleased or glad, be gracious or kind (with gen. ‘to favour’; with inf. ‘to deign to’; Impv. often ‘be so gracious, please’), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to be successful (as an action), Ragh. :
Caus. -सादयति (mc. also ˚ते; Pass. -साद्यते),
to make clear, purify, Kāvyād.; Kathās.;
to make serene, gladden (the heart), Bhartṛ.;
to render calm, soothe, appease, propitiate, ask a person (acc.)
to or for (inf. dat. loc., अर्थे with gen., or अर्थम् ifc.), Mn.; MBh. &c.

प्र-√ शम् P. -शाम्यति, to become calm or tranquil, be pacified or soothed, settle down (as dust), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to be allayed or extinguished, cease, disappear, fade away, ib. :
Caus. -शमयति (rarely शाम्˚), to appease, calm, quench, allay, extinguish, terminate, ib.;
to make subject, subdue, conquer, MBh.

प्र-√ शास् P. -शास्ति, (ep. also Ā.), to teach, instruct, direct, RV.; ŚBr.; R.;
to give instructions to, order, command (acc.), MBh.; R.; MārkP.;
to chastise, punish, MBh.; Kathās.;
to govern, rule, reign (also with राज्यम्), be lord of (acc. with or without अधि), ŚBr.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to decide upon (loc.), MBh.

प्र-√ सृ P. -सिसर्ति, (only Ved.) and सरति (sometimes also Ā. ˚ते), to move forwards, advance (‘for’ or ‘against’ acc.), proceed (lit. and fig.), spring up, come forth, issue from (abl.), appear, rise, spread, extend, RV. &c. &c.;
to break out (as fire, a disease &c.), MBh.; Pañcat. (v.l.);
to be displaced (as the humours of the boy), Suśr.;
to be diffused (as odour), Kathās.;
to pass, elapse (as night), Vikr.;
to commence, begin, Bhartṛ.; Kathās. (also Pass., e.g. प्रासारि याज्ञः, ‘the sacrifice began’, ŚBr.);
to prevail, hold good, take place, Sarvad.;
to stretch out (hands), RV.;
to agree, promise, Inscr. :
Caus. -सारयति, to stretch out, extend, VS. &c. &c.;
to spread out, expose (wares &c. for sale), Mn.; R. &c.;
to open wide (eyes, mouth, &c.), Mṛcch.; BhP.;
to diffuse, circulate, exhibit, Var.; Śaṃk.;
to prosecute, transact, Kād.;
 (in gram.) to change a semivowel into the corresponding vowel, Pat. :
Intens. (-सस्रे, ˚राते, ˚राण) to extend, be protracted, last, RV.

प्र-√ स्रु P. -स्रवति (rarely Ā. ˚ते), to flow forth, flow from (abl.), AV. &c. &c.;
to flow with, let flow, pour out (acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. Ā. -स्रावयते, to make water, ŚBr.

प्र-√ श्वस् P. -श्वसिति, to breathe in, inhale, MBh. :
Caus. -श्वासयति, to cause to breathe, ŚBr.;
to comfort, console, Hariv.

√ 1. प्राश् (प्र- 1. अश्) P. प्राश्नोति (aor. प्रानट्), to reach, attain, RV.;
to fall to the lot or share of (acc.), ib. :
Caus. प्राशापयति, to cause to reach or attain, MānGṛ.

√ (प्र- 2. अस्) P. प्रास्यति, to throw or hurl forth, throw into (loc.), cast, discharge (a missile), RV. &c. &c.;
to upset, Mn. xi, 176;
 (with अंशम्) to cast lots, lay a wager, TāṇḍBr.

प्र-√ सञ्ज् P. Ā. -सजति, ˚ते, (P.) to hang on, attach to (loc.), Lāṭy.;
to hang with i.e. to provide or supply with (instr.), ŚBr.;
to cling to (loc.), Daś.;
to engage with any one (loc.) in a quarrel or dispute, ChUp.;
 (only ind.p. -सज्य) to be attached to the world, BhP.;
to result, follow, be the consequence of anything, Sarvad.;
to cause to take place, Pat.;
 (Ā.) to attach one's self to (acc.), MBh. :
Pass. सज्यते, or -सज्जते (˚ति), to attach one's self, cling to, be devoted to or intent upon or occupied with (loc.), Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to be in love (pr.p. -सज्जन्ती), Hariv.;
 (-सज्जते), to be the consequence of something else, result, follow, be applicable, Pat.; Bhāṣāp.; Sarvad. :
Caus. P. -सञ्जयति, to cause to take place, Naiṣ.;
 Ā. -सज्जयते, to attach to, stick in (loc.; with न, ‘to fly through’, said of an arrow), R.

प्र-सम्-√ ईक्ष् Ā. -ईक्षते, to look at or upon, observe, perceive, see, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to wait for, BhP.;
to reflect upon, consider, deliberate, ib.;
to acknowledge, regard as (acc.), MBh.

प्र-√ सह् Ā. -सहते (rarely P. ˚ति: ind.p. -सह्य See below), to conquer, be victorious, RV.; AV.;
to bear up against, be a match for or able to withstand, sustain, endure (acc.), MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to check, restrain, R.;
to be able to (inf.), MBh.

प्र-√ साध् Caus. -साधयति, to reduce to obedience or subjection, subdue, TS.; Mn. &c.;
to reduce to order, arrange, settle, AV.; Kām.; Ragh.; Suśr.;
to adorn, decorate, Kāv.; Kathās.;
to manage, perform, execute, accomplish, RV. &c. &c.;
to gain, acquire, Vcar.; Pañcat.;
to find out by calculation, Gaṇit.;
to prove, demonstrate, Nīlak.

प्र-√ सिच् P. -सिञ्चति, to pour out, shed, emit, AV. &c. &c.;
to sprinkle, water, MBh.; Hariv.;
to fill (a vessel), KauṣUp.:
Pass. -सिच्यते, to be poured out or flow forth, MBh.; Suśr.;
to be watered i.e. refreshed, MBh. :
Caus. -सेचयति, to pour into (loc.), Yājñ.

प्र-√ 3. सिध् P. -सिध्यति, (rarely Ā. ते), to be accomplished or effected, succeed, Mn.; MBh. &c.;
to result from (abl.), Mn. xii, 97;
to be explained or made clear, Kāś. on Pāṇ. iii, 1, 122.

प्र-√ 1. सू P. -सुवति, -सौति, (Impv. -सुहि with v.l. -सूहि, KātyŚr.), to set in motion, rouse to activity, urge, incite, impel, bid, command, RV.; AV.; Br.;
to allow, give up to, deliver, AV.; Br.; ŚrS.;
to hurl, throw, Bhaṭṭ., Sch.

प्र-√ 2. सू Ā. -सूते, -सूयते, (rarely P. -सवति, -सौति; once Pot. -सुनुयात्, Vajracch.),
to procreate, beget, bring forth, obtain offspring or bear fruit, produce, Br.; Mn.; MBh. &c.;
 (mostly Ā. -सूयते, rarely ˚ति) to be born or produced, originate, arise, Mn.; MBh. &c.

प्र-√ सृज् P. -सृजति, (aor. P. -अस्राक् Ā. -असृक्षत), to let loose, dismiss, send off to (acc.), RV. &c. &c.;
to give free course to (anger &c., with acc.), MBh.;
to stretch out (the arms), RV.;
to scatter, sow, MārkP.;
to engage in a quarrel with (loc.), MBh. (prob. w.r. for प्र-सजति) :
Pass. -सृज्यते, to go forth or out, leave home, Gobh.; Lāṭy. :
Desid. -सिस्रिक्षति, to wish to dismiss or send off, ŚāṅkhBr.

प्र-√ सृप् P. -सर्पति, to creep up to, glide into (acc.), RV.; VS.; Br.; ŚrS.;
to advance, proceed, move towards (acc.), Vait.; MBh. &c.;
to stream or break forth, MBh.; Śiś. : to set in (as darkness), Kathās.;
to spread, extend, be diffused, Śatr.; Uttarar.;
to set to work, act, proceed in a certain way, Kām.; Kathās.;
to advance, progress, Bhaṭṭ.

प्र-√ स्कन्द् P. -स्कन्दति (ind.p. -स्कन्द्य, or -स्कद्य), to leap forth or out or up or down, TS.; Br.; MBh. &c.;
to gush forth (as tears), Gaut.;
to fall into (acc.), R.;
to fall upon, attack, MBh.;
to shed, spill, Br.; Up. :
Caus. -स्कन्दयति. to cause to flow (a river; others ‘to cross’), MBh.; Hariv.;
to pour out (as an oblation), MBh.

प्र-√ स्तु P. -स्तौति (in RV. also Ā. -स्तवते, with act. and pass. sense, and 1. sg. -स्तुषे), to praise before (anything else) or aloud, RV. &c. &c.;
to sing, chant (in general, esp. said of the Prastotṛ), Br.; Lāṭy.; ChUp.;
to come to speak of, introduce as a topic, Prab.; Hit.; BhP.;
to undertake, commence, begin, Mālav.; Dhūrtas.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to place at the head or at the beginning, Sarvad. :
Caus. -स्तावयति, to introduce as a topic, suggest, MBh.; Mālatīm.

प्र-√ स्तुभ् (only pr. p. Ā. -स्तुभान॑, with pass. sense), to urge on with shouts, RV. :
Caus. -स्तोभयति, to greet with shouts, BhP.;
to scoff, deride, insult, ib.

प्र-√ स्था P. -तिष्ठति, (rarely Ā. ते). to stand or rise up (esp. before the gods, an altar &c.), RV.; TS.; VS.;
to advance towards (acc.), ŚBr.; ŚāṅkhŚr.;
 (Ā.; cf. Pāṇ. i, 3, 22)
to be awake, MBh.;
 (Ā. mc. also P.) to set out, depart from (abl.), proceed or march to (acc. with or without प्रति) or with a view to or in order to (dat. or inf.), ĀśvGṛ.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
 (with आकाशे) to move or abide in the open air, R. :
Caus. -स्थापयति, to put aside, AV. ;
to send out, send to (acc. with or without प्रति) or for the purpose of (dat. or loc.), send away or home, dispatch messengers &c., dismiss, banish, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
 drive, urge on (horses), Kum. Desid. Ā. -तिष्ठासते, to wish to set out, Śaṃk.; Bhaṭṭ.

प्र-√ स्नु P. Ā. -स्नौति, -स्नुते, to emit fluid, pour forth, flow, drip, distil, TS.; Kathās.;
 (Ā.) to yield milk (aor. प्रास्नोष्ट), Pāṇ. iii, 1, 89, Sch.:
Desid. -सुस्नूषिष्यते, vii, 2, 36,

प्र-√ स्फुट् P. -स्फुटति, to burst open, be split or rent, MBh.; R. :
Caus. -स्फोटयति, to cleave through, split, pierce, Hariv.; Kathās.;
to slap or clap the arms, MBh.

प्र-√ स्फुर् P. -स्फुरति (pr. p. Ā. -स्फुरमाण, MBh.), to spurn or push away, AV.;
to become tremulous, throb, quiver, palpitate, RV. &c. &c.;
to glitter, sparkle, flash, shine forth (lit. and fig.), Hariv.; Kāv.; Kathās.;
to be displayed, become clear or visible, appear, Kāv.; Var.

प्र-√ स्यन्द् P. Ā. -स्यन्दति, ˚ते (often w.r. for -स्पन्द्), to flow forth, run away, dart, fly, RV.; GṛS.; MBh.;
to drive off (in a carriage), ŚBr. :
Caus. -स्यन्दयति, to make flow, MBh.
